rom bit 31)")) (step (n 30) (insn "sraiw x9, x8, 28") (writes (write (reg "x9") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF8"))) (derivation "shamt 28 of the 5-bit field: the low 32 bits 0x80000001 >> 28 ARITHMETIC, then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF8.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT: a 5-bit amount; D-WSUFFIX: sign-extend from bit 31)")) (step (n 31) (insn "sraiw x9, x8, 29") (writes (write (reg "x9") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC"))) (derivation "shamt 29 of the 5-bit field: the low 32 bits 0x80000001 >> 29 ARITHMETIC, then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT: a 5-bit amount; D-WSUFFIX: sign-extend from bit 31)")) (step (n 32) (insn "sraiw x9, x8, 30") (writes (write (reg "x9") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFE"))) (derivation "shamt 30 of the 5-bit field: the low 32 bits 0x80000001 >> 30 ARITHMETIC, then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFE.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT: a 5-bit amount; D-WSUFFIX: sign-extend from bit 31)")) (step (n 33) (insn "sraiw x9, x8, 31") (writes (write (reg "x9") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "shamt 31 of the 5-bit field: the low 32 bits 0x80000001 >> 31 ARITHMETIC, then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF. Bit 31 fills the whole word and the upper half.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT: a 5-bit amount; D-WSUFFIX: sign-extend from bit 31)")) (step (n 34) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 0") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0xFFFFFFFF80000001"))) (derivation "shamt 0: 0x80000001 >>> 0 = 0x80000001 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0xFFFFFFFF80000001.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 35) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 1") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0x0000000040000000"))) (derivation "shamt 1: 0x80000001 >>> 1 = 0x40000000 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0x0000000040000000. Bit 31 of the 32-bit result is CLEAR here — the upper half stays zero, unlike the sraiw sweep.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 36) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 2") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0x0000000020000000"))) (derivation "shamt 2: 0x80000001 >>> 2 = 0x20000000 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0x0000000020000000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 37) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 4") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0x0000000008000000"))) (derivation "shamt 4: 0x80000001 >>> 4 = 0x08000000 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0x0000000008000000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 38) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 8") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0x0000000000800000"))) (derivation "shamt 8: 0x80000001 >>> 8 = 0x00800000 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0x0000000000800000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 39) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 16") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0x0000000000008000"))) (derivation "shamt 16: 0x80000001 >>> 16 = 0x00008000 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0x0000000000008000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 40) (insn "srliw x20, x8, 31") (writes (write (reg "x20") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "shamt 31: 0x80000001 >>> 31 = 0x00000001 within 32 bits (zeros enter), then sign-extended from bit 31 = 0x0000000000000001.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 41) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 0") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0xFFFFFFFF80000001"))) (derivation "shamt 0: 0x80000001 << 0, low 32 bits kept = 0x80000001, sign-extended = 0xFFFFFFFF80000001.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 42) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 1") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000002"))) (derivation "shamt 1: 0x80000001 << 1, low 32 bits kept = 0x00000002, sign-extended = 0x0000000000000002.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 43) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 2") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000004"))) (derivation "shamt 2: 0x80000001 << 2, low 32 bits kept = 0x00000004, sign-extended = 0x0000000000000004.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 44) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 4") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000010"))) (derivation "shamt 4: 0x80000001 << 4, low 32 bits kept = 0x00000010, sign-extended = 0x0000000000000010.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 45) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 8") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000000100"))) (derivation "shamt 8: 0x80000001 << 8, low 32 bits kept = 0x00000100, sign-extended = 0x0000000000000100.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 46) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 16") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0x0000000000010000"))) (derivation "shamt 16: 0x80000001 << 16, low 32 bits kept = 0x00010000, sign-extended = 0x0000000000010000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 47) (insn "slliw x21, x8, 31") (writes (write (reg "x21") (value "0xFFFFFFFF80000000"))) (derivation "shamt 31: 0x80000001 << 31, low 32 bits kept = 0x80000000, sign-extended = 0xFFFFFFFF80000000. Bit 0 reaches bit 31, so the *W extension fills the upper half with ones.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.1 (D-SHAMT; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 48) (insn "addi x10, x0, 96") (writes (write (reg "x10") (value "0x0000000000000060"))) (derivation "96 = 0b1100000: the register whose low-6 and low-5 readings differ — 32 vs 0.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 49) (insn "srl x12, x8, x10") (writes (write (reg "x12") (value "0x00000000FFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "D-SHAMT: SRL reads the low 6 bits — 96 reads as 32 — so X >>> 32 = 0x00000000FFFFFFFF.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.2")) (step (n 50) (insn "addi x11, x0, 1") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "The pre-write: the next step is the identity under the 5-bit read, so x11 starts at 1 and the result lands as a transition.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 51) (insn "srlw x11, x8, x10") (writes (write (reg "x11") (value "0xFFFFFFFF80000001"))) (derivation "⭐ The discriminator: the SAME register pair, the *W form — the amount is rs2[4:0] = 0, so nothing shifts, and D-WSUFFIX sign-extends the low half: 0xFFFFFFFF80000001. Steps with srl/srlw on identical operands answer 0x00000000FFFFFFFF vs 0xFFFFFFFF80000001 — a 6-bit reader of the *W form would answer 0xFFFFFFFF80000000 for srlw by 32, and both differences are visible here.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.2 (the *W shifts use rs2[4:0]; D-WSUFFIX)")) (step (n 52) (insn "addi x13, x0, -1") (writes (write (reg "x13") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF: low 5 bits all ones — the maximum *W amount.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 53) (insn "sllw x14, x8, x13") (writes (write (reg "x14") (value "0xFFFFFFFF80000000"))) (derivation "The amount is rs2[4:0] = 31: 0x80000001 << 31 keeps only 0x80000000 in 32 bits, and the *W sign extension fills the upper half: 0xFFFFFFFF80000000.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.2")) (step (n 54) (insn "sraw x15, x8, x13") (writes (write (reg "x15") (value "0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF"))) (derivation "The same amount, arithmetic within 32 bits: bit 31 fills the word (0xFFFFFFFF), and the sign extension fills the upper half too: 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.") (source "RVI-RV64I §3.1.2.2")))
